Pi Piper

Pi Piper (earlier working names: Open Pi and Spindle) is an independent,
solo open-source framework for live performance on compatible pad
controllers. Pi Piper is compatible with Native Instruments Maschine
hardware. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by Native
Instruments / inMusic Brands, Inc. or their affiliates, and it is not made
by them. Maschine, Native Instruments, and related marks are trademarks of
their respective owners and are used solely to identify compatible
third-party hardware. Pi Piper does not ship Native Instruments logos,
branding, firmware, samples, fonts, manuals, or proprietary software.
Raspberry Pi is a trademark of Raspberry Pi Ltd.
Use of Pi Piper is at your own risk.

Compatible with Native Instruments Maschine Mikro MK3 and MK3 controllers.
Shift + Stop on the controller returns to the launcher.
